  "notes": "The half-time record its parent is not: the clap stack lands on beat 3 and the bar is felt at half speed, with 16th hats carrying the motion and sparse rolls answering into the next one. The backbeat is always a stack — snare plus clap plus snap — under a long clean reverb tail, which is the marker a 2020s mix leaves. Straight, quantized hard, and genuinely bimodal in mode as well as tempo: major and natural minor are weighted evenly, so the same beat reads bright or bruised depending on the seed. The topline is conversational rather than belted — short phrases, mostly steps, many syllables to the bar. The fast 160–175 half of the era lives in the drum-and-bass-pop mode, because a tempo block cannot state two humps.",
